# Milestone: M6 Wave 2
# Covers: Phase 9 (T94) Mutex primitive — cooperative single-VM lock.
#
# Mutex.new()       — fresh proto-clone with a hidden `_locked` slot.
# m.lock()          — sets _locked to true; returns nil.
# m.unlock()        — clears _locked; returns nil.
# m.tryLock()       — returns true and locks if free; returns false otherwise.
# m.locked()        — returns the current locked-state.
#
# v1.0 single-VM contract (URBI_SCHED_COOPERATIVE) means lock/unlock are
# non-blocking flag flips.  Cooperative wait via `waituntil m.locked() == false`
# lands at Phase 10's Mutex.synchronized .u overlay.

# Fresh mutex starts unlocked.
var m = Mutex.new(); m.locked()
[00000000] false

# Lock flips the flag.
m.lock(); m.locked()
[00000001] true

# Unlock flips it back.
m.unlock(); m.locked()
[00000002] false

# tryLock returns true on a free mutex and locks it.
m.tryLock()
[00000003] true

# Now locked, tryLock returns false without re-locking.
m.tryLock()
[00000004] false

# Unlock so subsequent tests can re-acquire.
m.unlock(); m.locked()
[00000005] false
